699	/**
700	 * Whether a URL addresses the bounded loopback origin the harness itself
701	 * serves. It is the one distinction that decides how a request is answered and
702	 * how it is written down, so it is exported rather than re-derived: the request
703	 * ledger records a loopback path exactly as requested and a non-loopback one
704	 * query-free, and both readings have to agree about which is which.
